[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ScatterDef" format=3]

; F-464/F-471 — the rubble a cliff sheds.
;
; A-016a built the rock vocabulary a year of terrain never placed: until this table,
; `terrain_accents` appeared in exactly one script in the whole repo, and that script was its own
; check. This is the first thing in the shipped game that puts one on the island.
;
; Biome-blind on purpose (`biome_id = "*"`): a cliff is a LANDFORM, not a biome, and the same face
; can run out of forest and into meadow along its own length. The slope floor is what makes that
; legitimate — see `ScatterDef.validation_errors()`. It sits at 30 degrees, a little under
; `ChunkMesher.ROCK_START_SLOPE_DEG` (40), so the rubble starts just before the ground itself turns
; to stone and there is no line where one begins and the other ends.
;
; Sparse (`coverage = 0.3` on a 7 m cell) and deliberately not dense: this dresses a face, it does not pave one. Steep
; ground is 0.4-2.2% of the island by `cliff_check`'s measure, so even at this density the table
; places a handful of pieces per cliff — which is what "the rock that fell off it" looks like.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://world/gen/scatter_entry.gd" id="1_entry"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://world/gen/scatter_def.gd" id="2_def"]

